      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'can you smell what the reich is cooking?' because the phrase uses the second-person pronoun 'you', directly addressing the viewer and inviting them to imagine or experience the implied sinister scenario. This creates an immersive and confrontational experience, making the user feel personally implicated in the meme's hateful message.",
